  ],
  "description": "Nobels ODR-1, schematic Rev. 5 dated 7 December 2000. The 250 kΩ Drive pot, 30 kΩ Spectrum pot and 50 kΩ Level pot follow the 11-pin control board wiring. Four 1N4148s implement feedback and shunt clipping. The Spectrum network includes the Q2 gyrator. BC264D, 2SK222E and 2SC2362G use BF245A, 2N5457 and 2SC2240 model substitutes respectively. The dry buffer remains as a load. Q5/Q7 use 60 Ω engaged resistances. Remote switching, flip-flop, LED and the open dry switch are omitted.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Drive",
      "Spectrum",
      "Level"
    ]
  },
  "name": "Nobels ODR-1 Natural Overdrive",
  "outputNode": "out",
